response.text:
- The expectations in the PRA’s Supervisory Statement apply to **all forms of outsourcing and, where indicated, other non‑outsourcing third‑party arrangements** entered into by PRA‑regulated firms【2†para 1.8】.  
- In developing those expectations the PRA took account of a range of international standards, including:  

  • the Basel Committee on Banking Supervision’s draft **“Principles for Operational Resilience”**;  
  • the Financial Stability Board’s **“Effective Practices for Cyber Incident Response and Recovery”**;  
  • the G‑7 **“Fundamental Elements for Third‑Party Cyber Risk Management in the Financial Sector”**; and  
  • the International Organisation of Securities Commissions’ draft **“Principles on Outsourcing”**【2†para 1.8】.
